{"archetypes":[{"name":"harness-api-fidelity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan names specific harness helpers and stub modes (write_sanitize_stub, run_subject_skip_path, assert_file_contains, GH_MODE=fail-injected, GH_FAIL_STDERR_FILE) that may not exist in the actual harness files; verifying these API claims against the real scaffold surfaces test-extension dead ends before any code is written.","prompt_body":"Read the actual test harness files (`skills/implement/scripts/test-generate-code-flow-diagram.sh` and `scripts/test-ci-failed-jobs.sh`) and check whether every helper function, stub mode, fixture path, and assertion API the plan proposes to use or extend is present and named correctly in those files. Flag any case where the plan assumes a function, mode, or assertion pattern that is absent, mis-spelled, or structurally incompatible with the harness already in place. Also verify that the plan's proposed new test block numbering (e.g., 'T8' in test-ci-failed-jobs.sh) does not collide with an existing block, and that the plan's description of what GH_MODE=fail currently exercises matches the actual stub logic. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
